Package: mcp-server-mastodon
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 python3-fastmcp (>= 2.0.0),
 python3-mastodon (>= 2.0.1),
 python3-dotenv (>= 1.0.1),
 python3-langdetect,
Provides: mastodon-mcp-server
Replaces: mastodon-mcp-server (<< 1.0.6~)
Breaks: mastodon-mcp-server (<< 1.0.6~)
Description: Model Context Protocol server for Mastodon integration
 A comprehensive MCP server providing access to Mastodon social network
 functionality through the Model Context Protocol, enabling AI assistants
 and other tools to interact with Mastodon instances.
 .
 Features include:
  * Timeline reading (home, local, public, hashtag)
  * Status posting, deleting, favouriting, and reblogging
  * Account management and social graph operations (follow, block, mute)
  * Notifications management
  * Full-text search for accounts, statuses, and hashtags
  * Trending tags, statuses, and links
  * List management
  * Media upload
  * Poll voting
  * Read-only mode for safe browsing
  * Support for both STDIO and HTTP transports

Package: mcprack-mcp-server-mastodon
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 mcprack (>= 1.5.1),
 mcp-server-mastodon (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: Registers Mastodon MCP server into mcprack catalog
 Companion package for mcp-server-mastodon. Installing it registers
 the mastodon-mcp binary as an available MCP server in the local
 mcprack instance; removing it unregisters it again.
